    {
      "vector_id": "jcs-depth-104-unbounded-recursion",
      "description": "Ten million nested arrays, about 20 MB of brackets. A canonicaliser that recurses once per level exhausts the call stack here rather than returning a rejection, and in a compiled runtime that unwind is not catchable. A byte cap alone does not close it: pure nesting stays small per level, so the input reaches any plausible size limit only long after it has passed any plausible stack. Refusal must be reached from the depth bound, before the recursive walk is entered.",
